From 3dccfc97ac1699a20ab83b5e1175f9a195725784 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:01:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(gateway): unchanged follow selection never
 rerolls a class allocation

commit_selection minted a fresh switch intent whenever [model, provider, physical, frozen pick]
changed or no memo existed, so a compaction (new physical target) or a first commit with no memo
replaced an unchanged class:deep allocation and moved the session to another provider with no
profile edit.

- Only a SELECTION change (tuple or the receipt's frozen pick) records a new intent. The memo is now
  {selection, physical}; a physical change with the same selection is a relocation: a still-pending
  intent moves to the new id as the SAME event (model_routing_switch_intent.relocate_in_transaction;
  record_in_transaction untouched), a consumed one stays consumed.
- No memo (first commit after upgrade): record the intent unless the lineage already runs a non-exact
  class allocation for the selected class. Exact selections and class selections over an exact pin
  still record it (pin correction / real first change).
- tests: unmanaged compaction / missing memo / both and managed compaction / missing memo keep the
  provider, allocation, allocator counters and fences unchanged, then still follow a real edit; a
  pending intent moved across compaction is consumed with its original event (no new order number);
  missing memo over an exact pin still moves off the pin.
